n%20microarrays.%20Bioinformatics30,%201363%E2%80%931369%20(2014).)\\]\n- 49.Xu, Z., Niu, L., Li, L. & Taylor, J. A. ENmix: a novel background correction method for Illumina HumanMethylation450 BeadChip. _Nucleic Acids Res._ **44**, e20 (2016).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkv907)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4756845/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26384415/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Xu,%20Z.,%20Niu,%20L.,%20Li,%20L.%20&%20Taylor,%20J.%20A.%20ENmix:%20a%20novel%20background%20correction%20method%20for%20Illumina%20HumanMethylation450%20BeadChip.%20Nucleic%20Acids%20Res.44,%20e20%20(2016).)\\]\n- 50.Foox, J. et al. The SEQC2 epigenomics quality control (EpiQC) study. _Genome Biol._ **22**, 332 (2021).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-021-02529-2)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8650396/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34872606/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Foox,%20J.%20et%20al.%20The%20SEQC2%20epigenomics%20quality%20control%20(EpiQC)%20study.%20Genome%20Biol.22,%20332%20(2021).)\\]\n- 51.Kirwan, J. A., Broadhurst, D. I., Davidson, R. L. & Viant, M. R. Characterising and correcting batch variation in an automated direct infusion mass spectrometry (DIMS) metabolomics workflow. _Anal. Bioanal. Chem._ **405**, 5147–5157 (2013).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00216-013-6856-7)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23455646/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Kirwan,%20J.%20A.,%20Broadhurst,%20D.%20I.,%20Davidson,%20R.%20L.%20&%20Viant,%20M.%20R.%20Characterising%20and%20correcting%20batch%20variation%20in%20an%20automated%20direct%20infusion%20mass%20spectrometry%20(DIMS)%20metabolomics%20workflow.%20Anal.%20Bioanal.%20Chem.405,%205147%E2%80%935157%20(2013).)\\]\n- 52.Broadhurst, D. et al. Guidelines and considerations for the use of system suitability and quality control samples in mass spectrometry assays applied in untargeted clinical metabolomic studies. _Metabolomics_ **14**, 72 (2018).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11306-018-1367-3)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5960010/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29805336/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Broadhurst,%20D.%20et%20al.%20Guidelines%20and%20considerations%20for%20the%20use%20of%20system%20suitability%20and%20quality%20control%20samples%20in%20mass%20spectrometry%20assays%20applied%20in%20untargeted%20clinical%20metabolomic%20studies.%20Metabolomics14,%2072%20(2018).)\\]\n- 53.All of Us Research Program Investigators; Denny, J. C. et al. The “All of Us” Research Program. _N. Engl. J. Med._ **381**, 668–676 (2019).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMsr1809937)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31412182/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?All%20of%20Us%20Research%20Program%20Investigators;%20Denny,%20J.%20C.%20et%20al.%20The%20%E2%80%9CAll%20of%20Us%E2%80%9D%20Research%20Program.%20N.%20Engl.%20J.%20Med.381,%20668%E2%80%93676%20(2019).)\\]\n- 54.Stang, P. E. et al. Advancing the science for active surveillance: rationale and design for the Observational Medical Outcomes Partnership. _Ann. Intern. Med._ **153**, 600–606 (2010).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.7326/0003-4819-153-9-201011020-00010)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21041580/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Stang,%20P.%20E.%20et%20al.%20Advancing%20the%20science%20for%20active%20surveillance:%20rationale%20and%20design%20for%20the%20Observational%20Medical%20Outcomes%20Partnership.%20Ann.%20Intern.%20Med.153,%20600%E2%80%93606%20(2010).)\\]\n- 55.Luo, Q. et al. A meta-analysis of immune-cell fractions at high resolution reveals novel associations with common phenotypes and health outcomes. _Genome Med._ **15**, 59 (2023).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-023-01211-5)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10388560/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37525279/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Luo,%20Q.%20et%20al.%20A%20meta-analysis%20of%20immune-cell%20fractions%20at%20high%20resolution%20reveals%20novel%20associations%20with%20common%20phenotypes%20and%20health%20outcomes.%20Genome%20Med.15,%2059%20(2023).)\\]\n- 56.Zheng, S. C., Breeze, C. E., Beck, S. & Teschendorff, A. E. Identification of differentially methylated cell types in epigenome-wide association studies. _Nat. Methods_ **15**, 1059–1066 (2018).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-018-0213-x)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6277016/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30504870/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Zheng,%20S.%20C.,%20Breeze,%20C.%20E.,%20Beck,%20S.%20&%20Teschendorff,%20A.%20E.%20Identification%20of%20differentially%20methylated%20cell%20types%20in%20epigenome-wide%20association%20studies.%20Nat.%20Methods15,%201059%E2%80%931066%20(2018).)\\]\n- 57.Faul, J. D. et al. Epigenetic-based age acceleration in a representative sample of older Americans: associations with aging-related morbidity and mortality. _Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA_ **120**, e2215840120 (2023).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2215840120)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9992763/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36802439/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Faul,%20J.%20D.%20et%20al.%20Epigenetic-based%20age%20acceleration%20in%20a%20representative%20sample%20of%20older%20Americans:%20associations%20with%20aging-related%20morbidity%20and%20mortality.%20Proc.%20Natl%20Acad.%20Sci.%20USA120,%20e2215840120%20(2023).)\\]\n- 58.Milbourn, H. et al. Generation Scotland: an update on Scotland’s longitudinal family health study. _BMJ Open_ **14**, e084719 (2024).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2024-084719)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11340249/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38908846/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Milbourn,%20H.%20et%20al.%20Generation%20Scotland:%20an%20update%20on%20Scotland%E2%80%99s%20longitudinal%20family%20health%20study.%20BMJ%20Open14,%20e084719%20(2024).)\\]\n- 59.Walker, R. M. et al. Data Resource Profile: whole blood DNA methylation resource in generation scotland (MeGS). _Int. J. Epidemiol._ **54**, dyaf091 (2025).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1093/ije/dyaf091)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12240559/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40633125/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Walker,%20R.%20M.%20et%20al.%20Data%20Resource%20Profile:%20whole%20blood%20DNA%20methylation%20resource%20in%20generation%20scotland%20(MeGS).%20Int.%20J.%20Epidemiol.54,%20dyaf091%20(2025).)\\]\n- 60.Kwon, D. & Belsky, D. W. A toolkit for quantification of biological age from blood chemistry and organ function test data: BioAge. _Geroscience_ 43, 2795–2808 (2021). \\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11357-021-00480-5)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8602613/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34725754/)\\]\n- 61.Tay, J. K., Narasimhan, B. & Hastie, T. Elastic net regularization paths for all generalized linear models. _J. Stat. Softw._ **106**, 1–31 (2023).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.18637/jss.v106.i01)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10153598/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37138589/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Tay,%20J.%20K.,%20Narasimhan,%20B.%20&%20Hastie,%20T.%20Elastic%20net%20regularization%20paths%20for%20all%20generalized%20linear%20models.%20J.%20Stat.%20Softw.106,%201%E2%80%9331%20(2023).)\\]\n- 62.Bernabeu, E. et al. Refining epigenetic prediction of chronological and biological age. _Genome Med._ **15**, 12 (2023).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-023-01161-y)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9976489/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36855161/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Bernabeu,%20E.%20et%20al.%20Refining%20epigenetic%20prediction%20of%20chronological%20and%20biological%20age.%20Genome%20Med.15,%2012%20(2023).)\\]\n- 63.Smirnov, D., Mazin, P., Osetrova, M., Stekolshchikova, E. & Khrameeva, E. The Hitchhiker’s Guide to untargeted lipidomics analysis: practical guidelines. _Metabolites_ **11**, 713 (2021).\n\\[ [DOI](https://doi.org/10.3390/metabo11110713)\\] \\[ [PMC free article](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8624948/)\\] \\[ [PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34822371/)\\] \\[ [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?Smirnov,%20D.,%20Mazin,%20P.,%20Osetrova,%20M.,%20Stekolshchikova,%20E.%20&%20Khrameeva,%20E.%20The%20Hitchhiker%E2%80%99s%20Guide%20to%20untargeted%20lipidomics%20analysis:%20practical%20guidelines.%20Metabolites11,%20713%20(2021).)\\]\n\n## Associated Data\n\n_This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article._\n\n### Supplementary Materials\n\n[Reporting Summary](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM1_ESM.pdf) (95.1KB, pdf)\n\n[Supplementary Table 1](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM2_ESM.xlsx) (13.3KB, xlsx)\n\nDemographics for the study populations used for developing and validating EMRAge, DNAmEMRAge and OMICmAge.\n\n[Supplementary Table 2](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx) (9.8KB, xlsx)\n\nThe extracted clinical phenotypes ( _N_ = 28) from the MGB Biobank.\n\n[Supplementary Table 3](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx) (18.2KB, xlsx)\n\nSelected clinical variables and their estimated weighting for calculation of EMRAge.\n\n[Supplementary Table 4](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM5_ESM.xlsx) (42.5KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs, ORs, _P_ values and standard deviations of associations between EMRAge, PhenoAge or chronological age and aging-related diseases in the MGB cohort. The models were adjusted for chronological age (if EMRAge or PhenoAge), sex, race, smoking status and alcohol consumption.\n\n[Supplementary Table 5](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM6_ESM.xlsx) (32KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs, ORs and _P_ values for EMRAge and PhenoAge, when both variables are included as predictors in a single linear model with aging-related health outcomes, in the MGB cohort. This model compares the relative effect sizes for EMRAge and PhenoAge when included together in one model. No additional adjustment for covariates is included in these models.\n\n[Supplementary Table 6](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM7_ESM.xlsx) (11.8KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs of one standard unit change of EMRAge, PhenoAge or chronological age to all-cause mortality or incident aging-related diseases in the All of Us cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 7](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM8_ESM.xlsx) (11.4KB, xlsx)\n\nORs of one standard unit change of EMRAge, PhenoAge or chronological age to prevalent aging-related diseases in the All of Us cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 8](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM9_ESM.xlsx) (10.9KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs of one standard unit change to all-cause mortality or incident aging-related diseases from joint analysis of EMRAge versus PhenoAge in the All of Us cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 9](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM10_ESM.xlsx) (10.6KB, xlsx)\n\nORs of one standard unit change to prevalent aging-related diseases from joint analysis of EMRAge versus PhenoAge in the All of Us cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 10](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM11_ESM.xlsx) (149.1KB, xlsx)\n\nInformation of the 2,430 multi-omic features compared to EMRAge for correlations.\n\n[Supplementary Table 11](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM12_ESM.xlsx) (52.7KB, xlsx)\n\nInformation of the 396 EBPs included as features in the predictive model for OMICmAge development.\n\n[Supplementary Table 12](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM13_ESM.xlsx) (38.6KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs of one unit/standard deviation change to disease for multiple aging biomarkers in the testing dataset of the MBG-ABC cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 13](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM14_ESM.xlsx) (14.8KB, xlsx)\n\nORs of one unit/standard deviation change to disease for multiple aging biomarkers in the testing dataset of MBG-ABC cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 14](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM15_ESM.xlsx) (14.6KB, xlsx)\n\nHRs of one unit/standard deviation change to disease for multiple aging biomarkers in the Generation Scotland cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 15](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM16_ESM.xlsx) (15.8KB, xlsx)\n\nORs of one unit/standard deviation change to disease for multiple aging biomarkers in the Generation Scotland cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 16](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM17_ESM.xlsx) (12.9KB, xlsx)\n\nORs of one unit/standard deviation change to disease for multiple aging biomarkers in the TruDiagnostic Biobank cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 17](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM18_ESM.xlsx) (35.9KB, xlsx)\n\nAssociation between OMICmAge and lifestyle factors in the testing dataset of MGB-ABC cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 18](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM19_ESM.xlsx) (12.2KB, xlsx)\n\nAssociation between OMICmAge and lifestyle factors in the TruDiagnostic Biobank cohort.\n\n[Supplementary Table 19](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM20_ESM.xlsx) (10KB, xlsx)\n\nICD-9/ICD-10 codes for clinical diagnosis extraction in MGB.\n\n[Supplementary Table 20](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM21_ESM.xlsx) (267.7KB, xlsx)\n\nSNOMED codes for aging-related diseases in All of Us.\n\n[Supplementary Table 21](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM22_ESM.xlsx) (441.6KB, xlsx)\n\nSNOMED codes for Charlson Comorbidity Index in All of Us.\n\n[Supplementary Table 22](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM23_ESM.xlsx) (343.6KB, xlsx)\n\nDiagnostic codes for aging-related diseases in GS cohort.\n\n[Source Data Extended Data Fig. 5](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/13004675/bin/43587_2026_1073_MOESM24_ESM.xlsx) (25.1KB, xlsx)\n\nTables of Pearson correlation coefficients and associated _P_ values on relationship between DNAm-based aging biomarkers and age, sex or immune cell fractions.\n\n### Data Availability Statement\n\nThe data used in this study were generated from two biobank cohorts housed at MGB and TruDiagnostic, respectively. Requests for raw data, analyzed data and materials used in MGB and TruDiagnostic Biobank cohorts to generate the results in this study will be reviewed by the contact PIs (J.L.-S. or V.B.D.). Due to participant consent restrictions, individual-level data linked to electronic health records cannot be made publicly available. However, we are committed to supporting scientific collaboration and transparency wherever possible. Researchers interested in noncommercial academic use of the data, algorithms or derived biomarkers are encouraged to contact the corresponding author (J.L.-S.) or first author (V.B.D., varun@trudiagnostic.com). Upon review, a collaborative agreement or data use agreement can be established to enable:\n\n• Access to de-identified omics data for research purposes\n\n• Application of algorithms or generation of derived biomarker scores on external datasets\n\n• Internal use of electronic health record-linked clinical data for validation, replication or joint analyses with external collaborators\n\nRequests will be assessed to determine whether they are subject to intellectual property or confidentiality obligations. Access to certain raw or analyzed data may be restricted if it relates to ongoing or future patent filings, or if release could compromise the commercialization strategy of MGB or TruDiagnostic. Access may also be limited for data containing proprietary algorithms or other commercially sensitive information. We welcome such requests and aim to respond within 30 days.\n\nPublicly available datasets referenced in this study include:\n\n• All of Us Research Program: [https://allofus.nih.gov/](https://allofus.nih.gov/)\n\n• Generation Scotland: [https://genscot.ed.ac.uk/](https://genscot.ed.ac.uk/)\n\n• SEER proteomics data for the MGB-ABC cohort are available under PRIDE accession [PXD048709](http://proteomecentral.proteomexchange.org/cgi/GetDataset?ID=PXD048709)\n\nCode to calculate all metrics is accessible via TruDiagnostic’s DNAm Analysis Software. You can request access to the software at [https://www.trudiagnostic.com/softwarerequest/](https://www.trudiagnostic.com/softwarerequest/), at no cost for research purposes. Access is contingent upon the requestor agreeing to a standard, noncommercial software license agreement that confirms the intended use is strictly for academic, nonprofit research and that the requestor will not attempt to reverse engineer or commercially exploit the software. All R codes used to develop and validate EMRAge, DNAmEMRAge and OMICmAge are available at [https://github.com/LaskySuLab/OMICmAge/](https://github.com/LaskySuLab/OMICmAge/).\n\n* * *\n\nArticles from Nature Aging are provided here courtesy of **Nature Publishing Group**\n\n![Close](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/close.svg)\n\n## ACTIONS\n\n- [![View on publisher site icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/launch.svg)View on publisher site](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43587-026-01073-7)\n- [![Download PDF icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/file_download.svg)PDF (5.2 MB)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/pdf/43587_2026_Article_1073.pdf)\n- ![Cite icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/format_quote.svg)Cite\n- ![Collections icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/action-bookmark-full.svg)![Collections icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/action-bookmark-empty.svg)Collections\n- ![Permalink icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/share.svg)Permalink\n\n\n\n\n## PERMALINK\n\n\n\n![Copy icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/content_copy.svg)Copy\n\n\n## RESOURCES\n\n### Similar articles\n\n### Cited by other articles\n\n### Links to NCBI Databases\n\n## On this page\n\n- [Abstract](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Abs1)\n- [Main](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec1)\n- [Results](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec2)\n- [Discussion](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec11)\n- [Methods](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec12)\n- [Supplementary information](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec38)\n- [Source data](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Sec39)\n- [Acknowledgements](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#ack1)\n- [Author contributions](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#notes1)\n- [Peer review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#notes2)\n- [Data availability](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#notes3)\n- [Code availability](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#notes4)\n- [Competing interests](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#FPar4)\n- [Footnotes](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#fn-group1)\n- [References](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#Bib1)\n- [Associated Data](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#_ad93_)\n\n## Cite\n\n![Close icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/close.svg)\n\n- ![Copy icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/content_copy.svg)Copy\n- [![Download icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/file_download.svg)Download .nbib.nbib](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/# \"Download a file for external citation management software\")\n- Format:\nAMA\n\nAPA\n\nMLA\n\nNLM\n\n\n\n## Add to Collections\n\nCreate a new collection\n\nAdd to an existing collection\n\nName your collection\n\\*\n\nChoose a collection\n\n\nUnable to load your collection due to an error\n\n[Please try again](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13004675/#)\n\nAdd\n\nCancel\n\n\nFollow NCBI\n\n\n[NCBI on X (formerly known as Twitter)](https://twitter.com/ncbi) [NCBI on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/ncbi.nlm) [NCBI on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/ncbinlm) [NCBI on GitHub](https://github.com/ncbi) [NCBI RSS feed](https://ncbiinsights.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/)\n\nConnect with NLM\n\n\n[NLM on X (formerly known as Twitter)](https://twitter.com/nlm_nih) [NLM on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/nationallibraryofmedicine) [NLM on YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/user/NLMNIH)\n\n[National Library of Medicine\\\\\n\\\\\n\\\\\n8600 Rockville Pike\\\\\n\\\\\nBethesda, MD 20894](https://www.google.com/maps/place/8600+Rockville+Pike,+Bethesda,+MD+20894/%4038.9959508,%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20-77.101021,17z/data%3D!3m1!4b1!4m5!3m4!1s0x89b7c95e25765ddb%3A0x19156f88b27635b8!8m2!3d38.9959508!%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%204d-77.0988323)\n\n- [Web Policies](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/web_policies.html)\n- [FOIA](https://www.nih.gov/institutes-nih/nih-office-director/office-communications-public-liaison/freedom-information-act-office)\n- [HHS Vulnerability Disclosure](https://www.hhs.gov/vulnerability-disclosure-policy/index.html)\n\n- [Help](https://support.nlm.nih.gov/)\n- [Accessibility](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/accessibility.html)\n- [Careers](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/careers/careers.html)\n\n- [NLM](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/)\n- [NIH](https://www.nih.gov/)\n- [HHS](https://www.hhs.gov/)\n- [USA.gov](https://www.usa.gov/)\n\nBack to Top![back to top icon](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/pd-medc-pmc-cloudpmc-viewer/production/9b1d9d87/var/data/static/img/usa-icons/arrow_upward.svg)","ra